eternalforest-by-soulman for Debian
----------------------------------

* The packaged executable is the debug build of the Makefile (make debug):
  the 4k version is linked by hand with an x86-64 _start entry point and raw
  syscalls, and compressed with xz behind a shell header that unpacks it to
  /tmp. The debug build is a normal GTK program, compiled with GCC instead of
  clang and the Debian build flags, so it is also built for the other
  architectures.
* The debug build reads the fragment shader at run time: it is installed as
  /usr/share/eternalforest-by-soulman/fshader.glsl. The upstream
  preprocessing of the shader with unifdef in a gen/ directory of the
  current directory, and the reload of the shader when it is edited, are
  removed (02_change-data-path.patch).
* Closing the window now stops the program, as the Escape key does
  (03_quit-on-window-close.patch).
* The icon is made from the upstream preview.png.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

